.TH ZIONSTATS 1 "2026-10-19" "zionstats 0.7.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zionstats \- btop-grade GPU observatory (SHM-backed TUI + headless daemon)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zionstats
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs the terminal UI by default, attaching to the shared-memory frames
published by
.BR zionstatsd (1).
With
.B \-\-daemon
it runs the headless daemon instead.  See
.BR zionstatsd (1)
for daemon-only options and the shared config file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-daemon
Run the headless daemon instead of the TUI.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interval " " \fISECONDS\fR
Sampling/refresh interval (floor 0.25).
.TP
.B \-\-demo
Synthetic four-GPU source (two NVIDIA, one AMD, one Intel); no hardware.
.TP
.B \-\-readonly
Forbid all actuation (structurally builds none).
.TP
.BI \-\-provider " AUTO|NVIDIA|AMD|INTEL"
GPU data source (default auto: NVML, then a drm vendor scan).
.TP
.BI \-\-replay " FILE"
Replay a recorded trace in the TUI (embedded replay daemon).
.TP
.BI \-\-record " FILE"
[daemon] record one Python-compatible frame per tick (ndjson or .gz).
.TP
.BI \-\-host " HOST" ", " \-\-port " PORT"
[daemon] metrics bind address (default 127.0.0.1:9400).
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Config path (default $ZION_CONFIG or ~/.config/zionstats/config.toml).
.TP
.BI \-\-mode " OFF|DRY_RUN|AUTO|MANUAL"
[daemon] cooling mode override.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-config
[daemon] print the resolved configuration and exit (never touches NVML).
.TP
.B \-\-completions " SHELL"
Emit shell completions and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The shared config lives at
.I ~/.config/zionstats/config.toml
(override with $ZION_CONFIG).  Keys are documented in the project README;
themes, plugs, cooling, weather, and export sections are shared with the
Python sibling.
.SH SECURITY
The metrics listener binds loopback by default.  Optionally set
[export] token (config only, never CLI) to require a Bearer token on
/metrics and /snapshot.  Plug control is LAN-local plaintext; see
SECURITY.md in the project tree.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR zionstatsd (1),
.BR zionstats-tui (1)
